<h2><strong>FAQs on SriLankan Airlines Business Class</strong></h2>
<h3><strong>Does SriLankan Airlines Business Class have lie-flat seats?&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, on the A330-200 and A330-300, both of which offer fully flat beds. The A321neo used on regional routes does not recline to fully flat, since it's built for shorter sectors.</span></p>
<h3><strong>Which SriLankan Airlines Business Class seat is the best?&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The A330-300's 1-2-1 reverse herringbone configuration is the strongest product in the fleet, offering direct aisle access for every passenger and a 2024 cabin refresh, though not every A330-300 has received the update yet.</span></p>
<h3><strong>Does SriLankan Airlines Business Class have Wi-Fi?&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Coverage is inconsistent. Wi-Fi is not available on the A330-200, and availability varies elsewhere across the fleet, so check your specific aircraft before you fly if staying connected matters.</span></p>
<h3><strong>What is the baggage allowance in SriLankan Airlines Business Class?&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">40kg checked baggage, plus two cabin bags up to 7kg each, compared to 30kg checked and one cabin bag in Economy.</span></p>
<h3><strong>Is SriLankan Airlines Business Class worth the price?&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It depends on the aircraft. The refreshed A330-300 offers a genuinely competitive long-haul product, while the older A330-200 and unrefreshed A330-300 cabins are comfortable but dated by 2026 standards.</span></p>
<h3><strong>Does SriLankan Airlines have airport lounges for Business Class passengers?&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, the Serendib Lounge at Bandaranaike International Airport in Colombo, which includes shower facilities. Access at other airports depends on local agreements and your specific routing.</span></p>
